Do not import the Harmony parser eagerly.

`vllm/parser/harmony.py` does a module-level
`from xgrammar.openai_tool_call_schema import ...`, which only exists from
xgrammar 0.1.34 onward. nixpkgs ships 0.1.33, and vLLM's own metadata pin
(`xgrammar >= 0.2.1`) is relaxed away by pythonRelaxDeps, so the mismatch
surfaces as a crash on startup rather than at dependency-check time:

    ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'xgrammar.openai_tool_call_schema'

Harmony is the GPT-OSS tool-call format. `vllm/parser/__init__.py` is the
only place that imports it eagerly; ParserManager re-imports the module
lazily inside `get_parser()` and only when the model is Harmony-format, so
a model that genuinely needs it still fails loudly and in the right place.

--- a/vllm/parser/__init__.py
+++ b/vllm/parser/__init__.py
@@ -5,7 +5,12 @@
     DelegatingParser,
     Parser,
 )
-from vllm.parser.harmony import HarmonyParser
+
+try:
+    from vllm.parser.harmony import HarmonyParser
+except ModuleNotFoundError:
+    HarmonyParser = None
+
 from vllm.parser.parser_manager import ParserManager
 
 __all__ = [
